{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460279-clan-disciplines-what-are-your-personal-changes-if-any","id":1460279,"title":"Clan Disciplines: What are your personal changes, if any?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-17T18:11:20-07:00","id":1460279,"title":"Clan Disciplines: What are your personal changes, if any?","content":"My personal example would be me gutting the Ravnos (I\u2019ve always found them bland, even when they tried their best to fix them) and replacing the Brujah\u2019s Celerity with Chimerstry. This is one part inspired by The Lost Boys but one part made because it gave the Brujah yet another tool to assert their will and utopia on reality as a whole. They have Presence to sway the emotions of both Kindred and Kine. They can smash and rip others apart with Potence. And with Chimerstry, they hold the reins to other people\u2019s perception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27075-malfean_gorool","name":"malfean_gorool","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-17T18:26:49-07:00","id":1460282,"title":"","content":"Gargoyles have Fortitude, Potence, and their own unique version of Protean, which replaces the third, fourth and fifth dot powers with being able to meld with buildings, growing working wings, and becoming a sun proof statue. <br /> <br /> Malkavians have their original Disciplines of Auspex, Dominate and Obfuscate, with most of the Dementation effects being combination/alloy powers of those three. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-17T18:29:53-07:00","id":1460283,"title":"","content":"<b>Malkavian:</b> Auspex, Dominate, and Obfuscate<br /> <br /> <b>Tzimisce:</b> Animalism, Dominate, and Protean<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-17T20:41:11-07:00","id":1460296,"title":"","content":"While I haven't made any alterations I have on occasion considered splitting Oblivion up into two disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-17T23:14:43-07:00","id":1460304,"title":"","content":"Most of what i have done is streamlining by cutting the signature disciplines and making them into devotions, variant powers or, in some specific instances, occult rituals in the vein of those used by Garou (or some Sabbat and lone kindred exposed to less well known esoteric practices). Unfinished, among other things, because i keep tweaking things here and there depending on what i feel like using as a clue or easter egg to some chronicle-specific lore change and so on.<br /> <br /> <b>Malkavian:</b> Auspex, <i>Dominate</i>, Obfuscate (Dementation is acessed through a background/merit called &quot;enlightened madness&quot;)<br /> <br /> <b>Tremere:</b> Auspex, <i>Fortitude</i>, Dominate (got tired of the whole clan being defined/typecast by Thaumaturgy. Not every clan member starts with it, learning requires at least some level of commitment &amp; trust by the right - or very wrong - people, represented by dots of Clan Prestige or Mentor. Blood Sorcery is its own thing and <b><i>nobody</i></b>'s discipline).<br /> <br /> <b>Assamite:</b> Celerity, Obfuscate and ????. Subsumed Quietus into Blood Sorcery, still undecided over which discipline to insert in its place.<br /> <br /> <b>Followers of Set:</b> Obfuscate, Presence, <i>Protean</i>.Setite's Protean 5 is Form of Dust/Sand. The heart extraction power is a ritual instead.<br /> <br /> <b>Giovanni:</b> Dominate, Potence, <i>Presence</i>. Necromancy might be either its own thing or more Blood Sorcery paths depending on my mood, but what goes for Tremere and Assamites with Blood Sorcery also applies here, you need to be converted/initiated into one of the clan's many cabals to get access to it. Inserting Presence in its place was something of a little wink to the Giovanni standing somewhere between Ventrue &amp; Lasombra.<br /> <br /> <b>Ravnos:</b> Animalism, Fortitude, Obfuscate. Chimerstry is simply an &quot;alternate path&quot; of Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> <b>Lasombra</b>: Dominate, Obfuscate, Potence. Shadowplay on itself is a group of alternate powers for Obfuscate. Arms of Ahriman and any other solid shadow/portal/etc weirdness i gatelocked into rituals from either the Amici Noctis, the Angellis Ater or other secret societies within the clan.<br /> <br /> <b>Tzimisce:</b> Animalism, Auspex, Protean. Zulo Form replaces one of the animal forms (in my own games the wolf form is closer to Garou's Hispo than normal wolf, so it kind of balances out, flight form can already become a &quot;chiropteran marauder lite&quot; in that it may turn into a man-sized bat thing instead of common bat). Fleshcrafts i made into a form of ritual occult art, what in retrospect makes a bunch of sense, imho.<br /> <br /> <br /> Extras:<br /> <b>Baali:</b> Baali in my games are a melange of Caitiff broods spawned/tainted by lingering Blood Bond ties to the cthonic will of dead Antediluvians turned wraith/spectre better known in the Underworld as Malfeans/Neverborn. Daimonon is not related to the demons of hell, but the powers of spectres &amp; Oblivion (also partly the reason some kindred are extra paranoid about the clanless).<br /> <br /> <b>True Brujah:</b> Temporis is &quot;just&quot; a extensive set of Auspex+Celerity devotions. In my own twisted setting the True Brujah are simply those among the Toreador that did not forget and mangle their ancient origins (far from the only ones, might be said. Almost all clans are mistaken or deluded in their belief the Antediluvians belong to any one clan in particular).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-22-2023, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T00:40:49-07:00","id":1460308,"title":"","content":"Temporis is just Celerity for narcisists (I'm not speeding myself up, I'm slowing the universe down!!!)<br /> <br /> Most of Mytherceria is an auspex Variation. anyone with access to changeling blood can learn it. Kiasyd thus have Auspex, Dominate and Obtenebration. Some of mytherceria is thrown into thaumaturgy/necromancy. <br /> <br /> Serpentis, thanatosis and visceraticka are all protean mutations, but they keep their distinct names and No Follower of Set will ever recognize they have the same discipline as the Gangrel. The Protean bloodlines can buy eachother's powers without conflict at in-clan rates, kinda like how elder disciplines work. They may be themed very differently, particularly with the FoS: a settite will likely turn to sand rather than ash with their thanatosis 3, Anyone learning serpentis powers without being apart of the FoS cult will likely avoid the snake thele in favour of other beasts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T02:28:34-07:00","id":1460312,"title":"","content":"I allow multiple powers to be learned at each Discipline level in my games. Similar to how V5 did it, but characters aren't restricted to just one power per level. Consequently, this has allowed me to excise all of the &quot;snowflake&quot; or clan-unique Disciplines and fold them into &quot;mainstream&quot; Disciplines. I've likewise turned lot of the more underwhelming elder powers into 1-5 dot powers.<br /> <br /> Discipline powers are divided into three categories: Common, Uncommon, and Rare.<br /> \u2022 Common powers can be learned without a teacher's instruction.<br /> \u2022 Uncommon powers require a teacher and include the likes of Chimerstry, Vicissitude, etc. A Gangrel with Protean can't spontaneously develop fleshcrafting powers. I've come up with a wide variety of Common and Uncommon powers, so the Ravnos and Tzimisce don't actually have &quot;more&quot; powers available to them.<br /> \u2022 Rare powers not only require a teacher, but are especially obscure and/or jealously guarded. Valeren/Obeah, for example, are rare Fortitude/Presence powers. While most any Tzimisce who wants to learn Fleshcraft can pick it up from a clanmate, and even non-clanmates who know a Tzimisce could potentially do so in return for favors owed, most vampires who want to learn Valeren/Obeah powers are out of luck.<br /> <br /> <br /> So with that in mind, I revised Discipline spreads as follows:<br /> <br /> <b>Assamite:</b> <i>Blood Sorcery (Dur-An-Ki)</i>, Celerity, Obfuscate. Castes are a social rather than &quot;biological&quot; distinction and have the same Disciplines.<br /> <br /> <b>Cappadocian: </b>Auspex, <i>Blood Sorcery (Necromancy)</i>, Fortitude<br /> <br /> <b>Giovanni: </b><i>Blood Sorcery (Necromancy)</i>, Dominate, Potence<br /> <br /> <b>Lasombra: </b><i>Blood Sorcery (Obtenebration)</i>, Dominate, Potence. Lasombra who pick up powers/rituals beyond the &quot;standard&quot; Obtenebration ones are considered Abyss mystics.<br /> <br /> <b>Malkavian</b>: Auspex, <i>Dominate</i>, Obfuscate. Dementation powers are Dominate powers.<br /> <br /> <b>Ravnos</b>: Animalism, Fortitude, <i>Obfuscate</i>. Chimerstry powers are Obfuscate powers.<br /> <br /> <b>Salubri: </b>Auspex, <i>Fortitude</i>, <i>Presence</i>. Valeren/Obeah powers are Fortitude and Presence powers. Castes are a social rather than &quot;biological&quot; distinction and have the same Disciplines.<br /> <br /> <b>Setite:</b> Obfuscate, Presence, <i>Protean</i>. Serpentis powers are Protean powers.<br /> <br /> <b>Tzimisce: </b>Animalism, Auspex, <i>Protean</i>. Vicissitude powers are Protean powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T05:59:23-07:00","id":1460320,"title":"","content":"The main alterations I made were;<br /> <br /> First, Dominate Malks are default (Dementation is just a weird Dominate/Auspex hybrid and the Malks already have Auspex).<br /> <br /> Second, changed Quietus and Vicissitude into blood magic paths and associated rituals (all those powers happen to already cost 1+BP to activate) and then made the Assamite spread Blood Sorcery (Dur-An-Ki), Celerity, Obfuscate and the Tzimisce spread Animalism, Auspex and Blood Sorcery (Koldunism).<br /> <br /> All the differences in castes and bloodlines within those clans then became totally cultural and path choices (the Old Clan\u2019s perferred first path is Corruption as it\u2019s basically \u201cDominate as used by an asshole\u201d though many also pick up Dominate cross-clan; it\u2019s a common discipline so not hard to find even just among other Tzimisce).<br /> <br /> The Wan-Kuei are also traditional vampires, but are a Sect, not a Clan; after the Flood, c. 14k years ago a forgotten Antediluvian traveled East and established his own brood. His Methuselahs became known as the Yama Kings and their clan came to be called the Akuma; their clan disciplines are Auspex (to identify wicked souls), Obfuscate (to move unseen) and Blood Sorcery (known as the Chi, Shintai, Soul and Demon Arts). Their clan weakness is a particularly clever and malicious Beast (basically the Po aspect) who takes control in a Frenzy. It is they who seek out wicked souls on the verge of death and feed them some of their blood as punishment for their sins in life; leaving them to wake starving an under influence of their Beasts and, since they were already low Humanity types in life, often leaves them as wights once the horror of what they do during that first Frenzy strikes.<br /> <br /> The Wan-Kuei is a Sect of survivors of this treatment who banded together and adopted their Dharmas (basically Paths of Enlightenment) to better resist their Beast. It is not that they cannot Embrace, it is like the Children of Osiris who choose not to. The Dharmas are not only the foundations of what their western cousins call Golconda (which allows one to surpass generational limit), but also the only known method that can pull a vampire out of wightdom (though only by adopting the path... not by returning to Humanity).<br /> <br /> Basically this gives a lot of the past flavor of Kindred of the East, but recontextualizes it into traditional Kindred lore so they\u2019re akin to the Laibon and Drowned Legacies rather than an entirely different type of supernatural entity.<br /> <br /> The final one is that the Baali became more like the Children of Osiris where most Baali are converts and Daimonion gets added on top of the previous clan\u2019s disciplines in exchange for the extra weakness to holy things. It makes their infiltration game easier (Tremere is no longer the only option for hiding their association) and provides a lot more flexibility in terms of villains (which to date is the only way I\u2019ve allowed them to be used in my campaigns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T13:01:51-07:00","id":1460360,"title":"","content":"I'm no good with power tinkering, but I've always thought it would be cool that Temporis was a Necromancy path, or that the True Brujah had Necromancy as a Discipline.<br /> <br /> Historians and philosophers with no moral qualms, studying the decay of civilizations, and retrieving long-lost artifacts from the Underworld ... or accelerating the inevitable fall and destruction of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T13:47:28-07:00","id":1460363,"title":"","content":"3rd/20th<br /> <br /> Samedi-I replaced Thanatosis with Necromancy since it's hands down the worst discipline, primary path is graves decay with bone and ash paths as auxiliaries<br /> Tremere- Path of blood must be taken as primary path unless you have a really good reason. i don't mind you having some obscure op path but I expect you to work for it.<br /> <br /> V5<br /> Oblivion re separated Necromancy and Obtenerbration as it serves no real benefit in game and creates too many issues with fluff. Removed the oblivion stain rules since they're not very good discipline as it is and the idea of certain disciplines being 'toxic/evil' then others is really dumb because they're all messed up when you think it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-18-2021, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T14:01:11-07:00","id":1460367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460279-clan-disciplines-what-are-your-personal-changes-if-any?p=1460320#post1460320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main alterations I made were;<br /> <br /> The Wan-Kuei are also traditional vampires....</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like a lot of what you've done here. I don't think i'd use it as you've written, but it is certainly good inspiration. The main issue (other than thinking the Hungry Ghosts as a pretty cool seperate splat) is that a lot of this stuff sounds too-great and you just have to ask yourself why wouldn't everything here easily spread outside of Asia. <br /> <br /> <br /> I actually use my Baali as just another bloodline. The idea that there's a Nephandi equivolent among vampires who need to consent to be embraced with an inherently evil discipline... just sounds wrong. Vampire isn't about heroes, it's about people with power abusing it. A fallen mage works. A fallen werewolf works. A fallen vampire? That's just standard. For me, Diaomonion works best if it's about as evil as Dominate; it isn't inherently, but you can abuse the hell out of it. Baali aren't evil because of blood, but they do walk a bit too close to the fire when it comes to demons, and when you derive a clan culture from that... you can imagine how things go bad. It's more interesting for me to watch things fall apart than to draw lines in the sand. <br /> <br /> <br /> Main topic: I don't think OCT should be Aus,Ani,Dom . It's a cool spread, but the Tzmisce are too disunified for Dominate to be standard. Fortitude or Potence would work best. In fact if there must be Vicissitude opponents among the Tzmisce, I think it'd be a good idea to give them a variety of replacements, to better suit the fact that Vicissitude is great and the Old Clan shouldn't really have legitimate claims to actually being &quot;old&quot;(er) <br /> The Bloodline with Ogham? I make Ogham Koldunic sorcery. I think they make more sense as a Tzmisce relative than a Gangrel one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T17:10:19-07:00","id":1460393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460279-clan-disciplines-what-are-your-personal-changes-if-any?p=1460304#post1460304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Assamite:</b> Celerity, Obfuscate and ????. Subsumed Quietus into Blood Sorcery, still undecided over which discipline to insert in its place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Auspex, perhaps? (as it ties in with the two non-warrior caste niches)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-19T05:00:54-07:00","id":1460419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460279-clan-disciplines-what-are-your-personal-changes-if-any?p=1460367#post1460367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like a lot of what you've done here. I don't think i'd use it as you've written, but it is certainly good inspiration. The main issue (other than thinking the Hungry Ghosts as a pretty cool seperate splat) is that a lot of this stuff sounds too-great and you just have to ask yourself why wouldn't everything here easily spread outside of Asia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it\u2019s one part cultural; once you call a place home for 10+ millennia you don\u2019t travel much.<br /> <br /> Another part is their Beasts are not mindless savages, but cunning serial killers and schemers and the majority of their low generations (the Yama Kings and Akuma) are absolutely lost to their Beasts. The only ones with control over their Beasts are the Wan-Kuei sect and part of their Dharmic path is to not Embrace others (its a 1 on the Path Sins for the Dharmas and I use the DAV method of the degeneration check being diff. 6+difference between current path rating and the sin).<br /> <br /> When everything lower than 7-8th Gen is basically a wight with good manners; and your non-wights are all Gen 8-13 who refuse to ghoul or embrace, that\u2019ll put a limit on how fast and far they can grow.<br /> <br /> At least that\u2019s how I do it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I actually use my Baali as just another bloodline. </div> </div> </div>My preferences for the Baali come from my first exposure to them being Shaitan in the Chaos Factor. I don\u2019t like all the myriad attempts to try and make the Baali playable (i.e. \u201cthey\u2019re only committing atrocities to keep even worse things from happening.\u201d). Mine exist entirely to try and release eldritch horrors to sink the world into sin and are prime example that no matter how wicked vampires think they are, there is always something that says \u201chold my beer.\u201d<br /> <br /> When a city even suspects a Baali is in town it\u2019s thinblood sacrifice! Camarilla and Sabbat living together! Mass hysteria! Break out the unlicensed nuclear accelerators time.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s nice to have a level of \u201cBig Bad\u201d between your run of the mill corrupt Elder and the blood god Antediluvians. Baali work really well for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-19T08:24:34-07:00","id":1460434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460279-clan-disciplines-what-are-your-personal-changes-if-any?p=1460312#post1460312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lasombra: Blood Sorcery (Obtenebration), Dominate, Potence. Lasombra who pick up powers/rituals beyond the &quot;standard&quot; Obtenebration ones are considered Abyss mystics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny enough, one thing I did for my Transylvania Chronicles game (other than a large-scale overhaul of how blood sorcery works) is similar. Lasombra learn Obtenebration by default, but with additional training, going on a relevant path, and re-attenuating, they &quot;upgrade&quot; Obtenebration into Abyss Mysticism and can learn relevant secondary paths and rituals without having to buy a completely separate discipline. One of the first, indicative, examples of how this impacts the disciplines altogether is I removed Shadowstep as an elder-level power altogether, and resolve Shadowstep as Path of Praapti.<br /> <br /> It allows Shadowstep at levels 1-5 but with caveats, and negates those ridiculous and horribly overpowered synergies between Shadowstep, Shadow Perspective, Darksight, and Shadow Lair. Even for elder powers, it's ridiculous the right combination of powers level 6 and 7 can replicate and exceed a published level 9 power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-19T14:54:52-07:00","id":1460470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460279-clan-disciplines-what-are-your-personal-changes-if-any?p=1460393#post1460393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Auspex, perhaps? (as it ties in with the two non-warrior caste niches)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Indeed. The fact it would subsume them as simply archetypes, factions &amp; fraternities within the bedrock of the clan instead of separate bloodlines does appeal to me too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T13:33:50-07:00","id":1460728,"title":"","content":"I like the Sabbat discipline spread for Ventrue and go with Auspex, Dominate, and Fortitude. Dominate/Presence are a bit over kill.<br /> <br /> I think DA Salubri with Auspex Fortitude and Presence using Combo Disciplines to heal body mind and spirit would work and get rid of Valeren (it has problems)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T04:10:10-07:00","id":1460811,"title":"","content":"Each vampire has access to Celerity, Fortitude, Potence, Protean, and 1 clan unique discipline which they should keep secret like an ace up their sleeve. <br /> <br /> Definitely adds more choices to players and combo powers are more accessible. Very interesting to see how players have decided to grow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19533-pnizzle","name":"Pnizzle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T05:27:22-07:00","id":1460816,"title":"","content":"If City Gangrel have to exist, they should have Animalism, Obfuscate, Protean. <br /> <br /> Celerity and Obfuscate together with a low-level aggravated damage dealing third Discipline is way too twinky, first of all. Second, a Gangrel without Animalism doesn\u2019t feel tight. Further, if they aren\u2019t out wandering the woods and wilds, they don\u2019t need the Fortitude as badly as they need to wander unseen among throngs of humans, which is the whole \u201curban predator\u201d angle. Of course, this makes them fairly close to Nosferatu, but that\u2019s preferable to \u201ceasier Assamite.\u201d<br /> <br /> Old Clan Tzimisce with Animalism, Auspex, Protean gives them the cool Dracula/Carmilla shapeshifting abilities while retaining the politicized rift between \u201cclean\u201d Old Clan and \u201ctainted\u201d Vicissitude wielders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-23T19:37:39-07:00","id":1461121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460279-clan-disciplines-what-are-your-personal-changes-if-any?p=1460728#post1460728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the Sabbat discipline spread for Ventrue and go with Auspex, Dominate, and Fortitude. Dominate/Presence are a bit over kill.<br /> <br /> I think DA Salubri with Auspex Fortitude and Presence using Combo Disciplines to heal body mind and spirit would work and get rid of Valeren (it has problems)</div> </div> </div> </div>After having played a Ventrue <i>antitribu</i>, I can honestly say it's one of my favorite discipline spreads in the game. At least, it's my favorite of any discipline spread that doesn't combine Auspex and Presence -- Toreador, Telyav, Szantovich (good god, <i>especially</i> Szantovich), DAV20 Assamite viziers...<br /> <br /> Ventrue, more than any other clan, <i>need</i> Auspex, and it's a shame that iteration is left to the <i>antitribu</i> bloodline. Who the <i>antitribu</i> really are, and how they ended up with <i>that</i> discipline via the Prayer to St. Gustav, makes for fantastic plot fodder though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T13:56:43-07:00","id":1461264,"title":"","content":"I think the Ventrue were deliberately given the weakness of not having Auspex because they were supposed to be less de facto intelligent than their main advisors: Tremere, Toreador, and Malkavians. The Ventrue are supposed to be the guy on the thrown, powerful but just a bit ignorant and disconnected. The three Auspex clans are supposed to be the guys whispering wisdom into Ventrue ears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T14:35:13-07:00","id":1461271,"title":"","content":"I reorganized the clan Disciplines for the chronicles I ST a long time ago. Strangely, some of the same ideas cropped up in V5. This is what I did:<br /> <br /> I gave the Malkavians their original Discipline set as I never liked Dementation. Auspex, Dominate, Obfuscate. <br /> <br /> I combined several Dementation and Chimestry powers into their own Discipline which was a &quot;secret&quot; Discipline only a few vampires knew that was rumored to be an Infernalist gift.<br /> <br /> So I had to find a substitute for it among the Ravnos. I gave them Animalism, Fortitude, Obfuscate. I never used Ravnos as NPCs and never had a PC play one, so I never got any complaints.<br /> <br /> I also combined Obtenebration and Mortis as the same Discipline. We'll call it Oblivion just to reflect V5 though it wasn't that. Though Necromancy itself was kept separate as its own thing that Giovanni (and other necromancers) could learn at Out Of Clan costs.<br /> <br /> So Lasombra had Dominate, Oblivion, and Potence.<br /> <br /> The Giovanni and Samedi had the same set as the Cappadocians. Auspex, Fortitude, and Oblivion. Although not that I had several discussions here about the Cappadocians, I'm thinking of changing that to Auspex, Potence, and Oblivion.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce had Animalism, Auspex, Protean. I never liked Vicissitude so I eliminated it in my games. I thought Protean was a sufficient substitute.<br /> <br /> I didn't like Serpentis or Quietus as their own Disciplines, so I made them their own set of Thaumaturgy Paths and rituals. So I just replaced their clan Disciplines of the Setites and Assamites with Thaumaturgy. They just had access to different Paths than the Tremere did.<br /> <br /> I never liked the idea of sub-clans within the same clan, so I eliminated as those as having any kind of Discipline difference or different clan weakness. Those bloodlines might still exist but as a particularly prestigious, infamous, or renowned lineage. But if you played Giovanni or Samedi besides the Cappadocian weakness, they all had to take a Flaw that simulated an additional curse.<br /> <br /> I only used other Bloodlines if there was a specific chronicle plot point that had to use them so I never put much thought into them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-25T00:52:19-07:00","id":1461310,"title":"","content":"Dominate, Fortitude, Presence specializes Ventrue into Director/Ruler types that can acquire allies and backgrounds as fast as conceivably possible. <br /> <br /> Auspex, Dominate, Fortitude... makes them exceedingly good cops and bodyguards, IE subservient. <br /> <br /> I'm sure you could probably make the case that Auspex, Dominate, and Presence (no Fortitude) would really be the ultimate people-winning bloodline. You could also argue that AntiVentrue make for better PCs and I might agree with you depending on the game's mood. But for the Ventrue, especially considering their weakness, Presence is a better trait than Auspex. For starters, Background accumulation is more important to Ventrue than discernment; Knowing how people truly feel is less important than knowing they're powerless to stop you, or knowing they're in love with you because you just Entranced them. Similarly, while you could say both Dominate and Presence create redundancies, I could say you don't need Auspex if you can just get someone else to use it. But most importantly, for me at least, and especially given the Ventrue's weakness, is that it's more important to be liked than to be intelligent. Charisma is just better for Ventrue than Perception, and the AntiVentrue really seem like they've gone the extra mile to be without charisma. Being a Ventrue is about talking your way into anybody's bed, not choosing who's got the best bed. <br /> <br /> I really do like the Antis, but they're a lesser product.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T07:29:56-07:00","id":1461552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460279-clan-disciplines-what-are-your-personal-changes-if-any?p=1461310#post1461310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Dominate, Fortitude, Presence specializes Ventrue into Director/Ruler types that can acquire allies and backgrounds as fast as conceivably possible.<br /> <br /> Auspex, Dominate, Fortitude... makes them exceedingly good cops and bodyguards, IE subservient.<br /> <br /> I'm sure you could probably make the case that Auspex, Dominate, and Presence (no Fortitude) would really be the ultimate people-winning bloodline. You could also argue that AntiVentrue make for better PCs and I might agree with you depending on the game's mood. But for the Ventrue, especially considering their weakness, Presence is a better trait than Auspex. For starters, Background accumulation is more important to Ventrue than discernment; Knowing how people truly feel is less important than knowing they're powerless to stop you, or knowing they're in love with you because you just Entranced them. Similarly, while you could say both Dominate and Presence create redundancies, I could say you don't need Auspex if you can just get someone else to use it. But most importantly, for me at least, and especially given the Ventrue's weakness, is that it's more important to be liked than to be intelligent. Charisma is just better for Ventrue than Perception, and the AntiVentrue really seem like they've gone the extra mile to be without charisma. Being a Ventrue is about talking your way into anybody's bed, not choosing who's got the best bed.<br /> <br /> I really do like the Antis, but they're a lesser product.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I will have to strongly disagree. our points of contention:<br /> <br /> Their weakness is trivial with Dominate command, feed, memory wipe. Enchantment is time consuming, do you really want to take the time to &quot;seduce&quot; a random mortal again?<br /> <br /> Presence does not really lend to background accumulation. The Enchantment ability would be a liability long term since the book specifically points out they get pissed off when it wares off. Even if you tried to renew it all the time, how often do you apply it and to how many people as your backgrounds grow?<br /> <br /> Where Auspex lets you know how they feel and even think for free when dealing with mortals, knowing what they really want and are really up to is far, far more useful when dealing with underlings.<br /> <br /> You can't really &quot;just&quot; get someone else to use Auspex for you, you are now dealing with a fellow Kindred whose powerful in his own right, and could just as easily mislead you, not to mention want something in return for service, and would not always be available.<br /> <br /> Ventrue are liked because they are smart social and likable as a rule, using Presence on your fellow vampires all the time will get you killed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T03:19:46-07:00","id":1461657,"title":"","content":"Dominate is more something you use if shit hits the fan or you want shit to hit the fan. You're underestimating Awe, which to be granted, isn't the best written discipline. But if you want to enrapture an audience, win a debate or rile people up, Awe is a strong carry. Awe is also subtle, you can get away with using it on other vampires.<br /> <br /> Entrance is strong because you can turn a stranger into your best friend <i>In a single turn</i>. This greatly simplifies the process of getting a blood bond because frankly, getting three drops of blood into someone on three different nights is a massive hassle, and with a few turns (or less if you're of low generation) you can make everyone in your room your <i>best friend, </i>Cornered by a group of thugs? Suddenly someone's advocating for you. You don't need to speak a word, worry about eye contact, whatever; you have an ally among your enemy getting you out of trouble. Presence works on animals, vampires with better generation, spirits, basically everything. Dominate is predictable, Presence isn't. Dominate can make people hate you, presence, yeah, they might hate you, but you've got plenty of time to avoid that.<br /> <br /> At low levels, Presence is more sustainable, though Dominate is cheaper.<br /> <br /> A good Ventrue will understand that leading people isn't about telling people what to do, but actually making them want to please you. It's about ballance, knowing when to carrot and when to stick. AntiVentrue don't have that ballance, they're all nutters.<br /> <br /> Curiously, I just read the 2e writup for Ventrue. It sells them really well as social, charming people. Dominate isn't social or charming. Auspex doesn't correlate to social clans, but everyone with Presence? They're highly social and charming. Sometimes you gotta think less like an optimizer and more about what feels right for the clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T07:38:01-07:00","id":1461680,"title":"","content":"I don't underestimate Awe, With other vampires it's just subtle and inoffensive enough to use in a debate because it doesn't target any one person. Using Enchantment to get one of the group you are arguing with on to your side will get you killed in the long run. Vampires don't like to be abused, and enthralling someone in Elysium isn't going to be looked at any more kindly than Dominating them or stabbing them with a sword in Elysium is.<br /> <br /> Blood Bonding again both get the job done, Dominate does so far more efficiently. Command: drink, mind wipe rinse and repeat two more times. Presence: come on, you know I love you. drink my blood and I know you love me too. I'd say with a vampire who knows what the Blood Bond is even enthralled they will resist.<br /> <br /> Presence as a weapon in a fight is great, but accumulating backgrounds and and winning arguments in Primogen meetings it is not so great at in practice.<br /> <br /> Knowledge is power, and Auspex gives you a great deal of knowledge (doubly so when dealing with mortals and willpower free mind reading) Knowing what it would take to turn someone to your side knowing what they are frustrated about on their side, a weakness they are trying to hide, or how to put the screws to someone is something that should not be underestimated. If I know your secrets I have power over you.<br /> <br /> Nothing wrong with presence, maybe we just see the chaos of presence vs the exacting nature of dominate with different values. Presence level 5 is amazing, but saps willpower too much to use all the time. Summoning is great if someone wanted to run and hide from you, instantly making someone your friend is great if they don't matter long term, scaring an attacker you don't want to fight into fleeing is cool, Awe is good for debates. I just don't see how it's required for leading and find Auspex far more useful in keeping everything under control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T09:14:00-07:00","id":1461698,"title":"","content":"Convincing a load of suckers to invest in a company? Presence. <br /> Convincing a load of suckers to take action against X? Presence. <br /> <br /> It's a good money maker. I don't think Dominate works so well when you are selling risky stock options. <br /> <br /> You can slip vitae into drinks (pre-v5) and Presence us great for getting drinks into people. Sometimes you just need allies NOW and you can work on the long term later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T10:37:25-07:00","id":1461713,"title":"","content":"I think we must agree to disagree. I like Presence, it's really useful, I just don't think it's needed to rule a vampire sect and in the halls of power where the running of things actually transpires I see Auspex as more useful, all the way down to running your personal henchman. Do the Toreador lead the Sabbat or do the Lasombra? Do Brujah run the Camarilla or do the Ventrue. How the clan is structured and who they choose to embrace are just as important as the Discipline spread. Presence is a great tool/weapon, but not why a vampire rises to prince as much as what he does/cares about and works towards.<br /> <br /> I personally find Dominate/Presence overkill and see more versatility in Auspex Dominate, but it's just my view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","user":"Vamps Like Us","date":". 09-27-2021, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T11:06:08-07:00","id":1461719,"title":"","content":"OK I tried to resist, I can't. Why is making money easier for Presence.<br /> <br /> Presence: it's a great oppertunity, go buy some xyz stock you'll be rich in no time. how much do they buy?<br /> Dominate: Call your broker, buy 10,000 shares of xyz stock, you came up with this idea watching the news. when it all goes south they blame themselves.<br /> <br /> Convince a load of suckers to take action against x. with what? Enthrall? one at a time, how is this different than Dominate, Awe? ok you have their attention, how they react will differ by individual, paying attention is not following direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T12:59:30-07:00","id":1461751,"title":"","content":"The Ventrue in the Camarilla are the Glue that keeps everyone together. <br /> The Ventrue in the Sabbat are... there. A funny footnote. <br /> <br /> Dominate has some rules against self harm. Your ST might be against you Dominating someone into investing into something any sane investor would be hedging. There's also humanity to consider. Screwing a guy to ruin with Dominate is a pretty serious morality infraction, and you're more likely to get a hunter from it. You can't really do it that often. Convincing many people into smaller losses isnt' half as bad and they still have freedom of choice. <br /> <br /> Awe is just better in repeat business than mesmorize or forgetful mind. <br /> Bah... <br /> If auspex gave you premonitions about market fluctuations, I'd see your point. But reading minds (a 4th level power) is worse than Presence's ability to turn the charm on. It's kinda difficult to articulate, but being the guy people follow (presence) rather than being the guy that follows others (auspex) is really good for Ventrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T13:31:57-07:00","id":1461757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460279-clan-disciplines-what-are-your-personal-changes-if-any?p=1461751#post1461751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dominate has some rules against self harm. Your ST might be against you Dominating someone into investing into something any sane investor would be hedging. There's also humanity to consider. Screwing a guy to ruin with Dominate is a pretty serious morality infraction, and you're more likely to get a hunter from it. You can't really do it that often. Convincing many people into smaller losses isn't half as bad and they still have freedom of choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being Dominated into thinking you found a great stock to invest in is not self harm, what a stretch. I guess Dominate never works. Go beat that guy up...well that's against the law, I could go to jail, self harm. Self harm is stabbing yourself or running into a fire...<br /> <br /> I guess the guy with Presence is making lots of humanity rolls instead of just one. Stealing is stealing, he's just stealing from 10 people. And again if using Awe and it's such an obviously sketchy stock why would they buy any? Use Enthrall and you have a whole bunch of other problems. Knowing if someone is sell you on BS is good, or how much money they have to invest in yours (Auspex).<br /> <br /> Get a hunter on you for using Dominate to change his memory of what happened to think he came up with the idea to invest in a stock watching the news? How does that make sense. Again I'm just pointing out your examples of things Presence can do, can all be done with Dominate, I'd argue with better results.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T13:58:47-07:00","id":1461761,"title":"","content":"I should admit, I also find Dominate to be really over powered and even made a thread about it. I pointed out the fact that all the advanced discipline dots past 6 just make your range better or let you hit multiple targets at once because they front loaded sooo much power into the first three dots. Everyone thought I was wrong. If it goes against nature their is a penalty? So what I think, humans have terrible Willpower for the most part, and a player with a little imagination can avoid the penalty, (and Auspex would be great for zeroing in on someone's Nature <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. The generation thing, not hard to buy the generation merit. The guy with Presence isn't going to do anything to a low gen elder either.<br /> <br /> Presence has it's uses, but unless you have endless dots in Disciplines, investing big in Dominate and Presence is over kill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T18:40:53-07:00","id":1461786,"title":"","content":"Dominate and Presence are both good in their own ways and I\u2019d be hard pressed to say which one is better. I do, however, think that having both Disciplines is a bit redundant. Not entirely redundant, mind you, because they are different, but redundant enough that I see having both Disciplines as a minor weakness for the Ventrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}